0.0</span></div><h3 class="font-display text-sm font-semibold text-[#181715] mt-1 leading-snug">Relating to public education and public school finance, teacher compensation allotments, and special education funding.</h3><p class="text-xs text-[#57534E] mt-1.5 line-clamp-2 leading-relaxed">Enacts an $8.5 billion biennial investment in Texas public education, increasing the basic allotment, creating tiered teacher retention allotments based on district size and tenure, reforming special education intensity weights, and expanding prekindergarten and career technical allotments.</p><div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-[11px] text-[#78716C] font-mono tabular-nums"><span>Author: Buckley</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>4 versions</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>2 linked</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>2025-06-20</span></div></button><button type="button" class="w-full p-4 text-left transition-colors cursor-pointer block hover:bg-[#FBF9F5]"><div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-[#57534E]"><div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 min-w-0 flex-wrap"><span class="font-semibold text-[#9A3412]">89R</span><span class="font-semibold text-[#181715]">SB 1</span><span title="Passed · Signed (Line-Item Veto)" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-1.5 py-0.5 border rounded-[2px] font-mono text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-wide leading-none whitespace-nowrap bg-[#F0FDF4] text-[#14532D] border-[#BBF7D0] "><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-[1px] shrink-0 bg-[#14532D]" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>PASSED</span></span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Senate</span></div><span class="tabular-nums font-medium text-[#181715] shrink-0">IDX 72.4</span></div><h3 class="font-display text-sm font-semibold text-[#181715] mt-1 leading-snug">General Appropriations Bill for the 2026–2027 Fiscal Biennium.</h3><p class="text-xs text-[#57534E] mt-1.5 line-clamp-2 leading-relaxed">Sets the $338 billion two-year Texas state operating budget, including $51 billion for property tax relief, $8.5 billion for public education (HB 2), $1 billion for Education Freedom Accounts (SB 2), Texas Water Fund capitalization, and Texas Energy Fund grid loans.</p><div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-[11px] text-[#78716C] font-mono tabular-nums"><span>Author: Huffman</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>2 versions</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>3 linked</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>2025-06-21</span></div></button><button type="button" class="w-full p-4 text-left transition-colors cursor-pointer block hover:bg-[#FBF9F5]"><div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-[#57534E]"><div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 min-w-0 flex-wrap"><span class="font-semibold text-[#9A3412]">89R</span><span class="font-semibold text-[#181715]">SB 2</span><span title="Passed · Signed" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-1.5 py-0.5 border rounded-[2px] font-mono text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-wide leading-none whitespace-nowrap bg-[#F0FDF4] text-[#14532D] border-[#BBF7D0] "><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-[1px] shrink-0 bg-[#14532D]" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>PASSED</span></span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Senate</span></div><span class="tabular-nums font-medium text-[#181715] shrink-0">IDX 71.3</span></div><h3 class="font-display text-sm font-semibold text-[#181715] mt-1 leading-snug">Relating to the establishment of the Texas Education Freedom Accounts program for eligible private and specialized educational expenses.</h3><p class="text-xs text-[#57534E] mt-1.5 line-clamp-2 leading-relaxed">Creates a $1 billion statewide education savings account (school voucher) program administered by the Comptroller, providing up to $10,000 per participating student for accredited private tuition, instructional materials, and therapies for students with disabilities.</p><div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-[11px] text-[#78716C] font-mono tabular-nums"><span>Author: Creighton</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>3 versions</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>2 linked</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>2025-05-03</span></div></button><button type="button" class="w-full p-4 text-left transition-colors cursor-pointer block bg-[#F4F0E8]"><div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-[#57534E]"><div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 min-w-0 flex-wrap"><span class="font-semibold text-[#9A3412]">89R</span><span class="font-semibold text-[#181715]">HB 14</span><span title="Passed · Signed" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-1.5 py-0.5 border rounded-[2px] font-mono text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-wide leading-none whitespace-nowrap bg-[#F0FDF4] text-[#14532D] border-[#BBF7D0] "><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-[1px] shrink-0 bg-[#14532D]" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>PASSED</span></span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>House</span></div><span class="tabular-nums font-medium text-[#181715] shrink-0">IDX 67.0</span></div><h3 class="font-display text-sm font-semibold text-[#181715] mt-1 leading-snug">Relating to support for the development of the nuclear energy and advanced reactor industry for electric grid reliability.</h3><p class="text-xs text-[#57534E] mt-1.5 line-clamp-2 leading-relaxed">Establishes the Texas Advanced Nuclear Energy Office and a $350 million matching grant fund within the Governor’s Office to accelerate small modular reactor (SMR) permitting, grid interconnection inside ERCOT, and nuclear workforce pipelines.</p><div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-[11px] text-[#78716C] font-mono tabular-nums"><span>Author: Harris, Cody</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>2 versions</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>2 linked</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>2025-06-14</span></div></butt